    "c1": {
      "anchor": "markup#table-1",
      "kind": "table",
      "label": "2. The markup: a sketch",
      "excerpt": "On Attribute What it does <ui-tour> name the title the gallery and the popup sho",
      "text": "not the friendliest name",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-20T01:48:28.902Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "scrim=\"none\"",
      "offset": 133,
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-20T02:07:21.094Z",
          "html": "<p>Renamed: P40 drops <code>scrim</code>. Dimming is off by default, and <code>dim</code> turns it on (<code>&lt;ui-tour-step dim&gt;</code>).</p><p>The other name, <code>spotlight</code>, is J244 on the epic page.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c2": {
      "anchor": "markup#table-1",
      "kind": "table",
      "label": "2. The markup: a sketch",
      "excerpt": "On Attribute What it does <ui-tour> name the title the gallery and the popup sho",
      "text": "remember = browser storage, `remember=\"on server\"`",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-20T01:48:38.908Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "remember",
      "offset": 146,
      "edited": "2026-11-20T01:48:57.040Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-20T02:07:24.508Z",
          "html": "<p>Done that way in P40: the bare <code>remember</code> keeps \"seen\" in this browser;</p><p><code>remember=\"on server\"</code> keeps it with the person's account, so it follows them to other machines.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c3": {
      "anchor": "markup#table-1",
      "kind": "table",
      "label": "2. The markup: a sketch",
      "excerpt": "On Attribute What it does <ui-tour> name the title the gallery and the popup sho",
      "text": "I'm assuming this is relative to the `target`.  If no target, it should be relative to the screen (under the Spell editor chrome).",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-20T01:49:29.693Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "ui-popup",
      "offset": 432,
      "edited": "2026-11-20T01:50:17.727Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-20T02:07:27.435Z",
          "html": "<p>Yes: the popup sits beside its target.</p><p>A step with no target is placed on the screen, under the editor's own bars. That's in P40's plan now.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c4": {
      "anchor": "markup#table-1",
      "kind": "table",
      "label": "2. The markup: a sketch",
      "excerpt": "On Attribute What it does <ui-tour> name the title the gallery and the popup sho",
      "text": "better name",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-20T01:50:27.122Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "scrim",
      "offset": 451,
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-20T02:07:30.895Z",
          "html": "<p>P40 calls it <code>dim</code>, a plain yes / no, off by default;</p><p><code>spotlight</code> is the other choice, in J244 on the epic page.</p>"
        }
      ]
    },
